# Third-party notices

This project ships one data artifact derived from a third-party MIT-licensed library.

## agency-agents-zh

- Source: https://github.com/jnMetaCode/agency-agents-zh
- Upstream: https://github.com/msitarzewski/agency-agents
- License: MIT
- Copyright (c) 2025 Michael Sitarzewski (original English version)
- Copyright (c) 2026 jnMetaCode (Chinese translation and localization)

`config/agency_personas.json` contains **compact role cards** extracted deterministically from
those role definitions (name / role / worldview / strengths / style). The upstream long-form role
files are **not** vendored; only the extracted cards are included, under the MIT terms above with
the copyright notices retained.

The cards are an **opt-in** library: no council uses them unless the caller explicitly adds one
via run_roundtable `add_personas=[{"agency_id": "<id>"}]`.

To refresh:

```bash
git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/jnMetaCode/agency-agents-zh.git
python scripts/import_agency_personas.py --agency-root ./agency-agents-zh
```

Deleting `config/agency_personas.json` simply disables the library; the MCP keeps working and
`list_agents(source="agency")` returns an empty list.